{
    "type": "game",
    "name": "Do U Copy?",
    "steam_appid": 1806420,
    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<strong><i>Do U Copy?</i> requires a minimum of 2 players to be played.  Get the Hacker App on our website</strong><br><br>Gear up for <i>Do U Copy?</i>, not your average VR co-op game - it's a party in a headset! Ideal for friends who argue over pizza toppings, families who can't assemble IKEA furniture without a feud, and couples who think they've mastered the art of 'unspoken communication'.<br><br><i>Do U Copy?</i> is the perfect blend of chaos, strategy, and teamwork to put your communication skills to the test! <br><br>Play as the <strong>Thief </strong>and make your way through one of the (least) secured banks in the country. Avoid traps, guards and camera using your VR legs and the guidance of your \u00ab guy-in-the-chair \u00bb.<br><br>OR<br><br>Play as the <strong>Hacker</strong>, become the eyes and ears of the operations through your phone, tablet or laptop! Using your (un)realistic skills, hack through the bank securities, guide your ally and solve engaging puzzles with unexpected turns!<br><br>Together, you'll fumble, bumble, and stumble your way through the heist of the century. Will you pull off the ultimate heist or just end up virtually 'breaking' a window? <br>Dive into <i>Do U Copy?</i> and find out! <br><br><i>Do U Copy?</i> requires a minimum of 2 players to be played.  <strong>Get the Hacker App on our website</strong><br><br>CREDITS : <br><br>Creative Director : Ilann Sayag<br>Technical Lead : Juan Ignacio Molteni<br>Lead Dev : Gaspard Delfosse<br>Lead Art : Vicky Tronc<br>3D Artist : Julien David <br>Game Design: Adrien Gabison &amp; Lola Zaluski<br>Narrative Design : Audrey Gravier<br>Composer: Jules &quot;JeuneOji&quot; Vidal<br>Special thanks to the ProtubeVR team and Plaine Image incubator.<br><br><br>Huge props to Mickael Z. for unifying our Game Design vision and mecanics post-Early Access.",
    "about_the_game": "<strong><i>Do U Copy?</i> requires a minimum of 2 players to be played.  Get the Hacker App on our website</strong><br><br>Gear up for <i>Do U Copy?</i>, not your average VR co-op game - it's a party in a headset! Ideal for friends who argue over pizza toppings, families who can't assemble IKEA furniture without a feud, and couples who think they've mastered the art of 'unspoken communication'.<br><br><i>Do U Copy?</i> is the perfect blend of chaos, strategy, and teamwork to put your communication skills to the test! <br><br>Play as the <strong>Thief </strong>and make your way through one of the (least) secured banks in the country. Avoid traps, guards and camera using your VR legs and the guidance of your \u00ab guy-in-the-chair \u00bb.<br><br>OR<br><br>Play as the <strong>Hacker</strong>, become the eyes and ears of the operations through your phone, tablet or laptop! Using your (un)realistic skills, hack through the bank securities, guide your ally and solve engaging puzzles with unexpected turns!<br><br>Together, you'll fumble, bumble, and stumble your way through the heist of the century. Will you pull off the ultimate heist or just end up virtually 'breaking' a window? <br>Dive into <i>Do U Copy?</i> and find out! <br><br><i>Do U Copy?</i> requires a minimum of 2 players to be played.  <strong>Get the Hacker App on our website</strong><br><br>CREDITS : <br><br>Creative Director : Ilann Sayag<br>Technical Lead : Juan Ignacio Molteni<br>Lead Dev : Gaspard Delfosse<br>Lead Art : Vicky Tronc<br>3D Artist : Julien David <br>Game Design: Adrien Gabison &amp; Lola Zaluski<br>Narrative Design : Audrey Gravier<br>Composer: Jules &quot;JeuneOji&quot; Vidal<br>Special thanks to the ProtubeVR team and Plaine Image incubator.<br><br><br>Huge props to Mickael Z. for unifying our Game Design vision and mecanics post-Early Access.",
    "short_description": "Do U Copy? is a VR co-op game ideal for parties, designed for friends, families, and couples. It challenges players with bank heists, where one is a VR Thief and the other a Hacker on PC/Mobile. Teamwork and strategy are key to success in this exciting heist adventure.",
